<description>&lt;p&gt;Bandits have intensified attacks in Niger, killing village heads, beheading leaders, burning houses and a palace, and abducting residents in villages such as Lumma Ba’are and Borgu. The Burkina Faso junta is accused of targeting journalists, activists and opposition exiles abroad. Human Rights Watch reports these repressive actions against media and civil society. The conflict continues to generate high mortality, with 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP. Recent incidents show a surge in bandit violence and state repression alongside the ongoing jihadist threat in the Sahel.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxOMkdOUkUxZjJrdEJpaEk2bkZuQUxtSklMZDg5bVNJc2xJNjBKQng1NU96RjJCRkV4WkJzekJra2dHTDNxTVh3WTJsMThzOWtlUC0yY0hHb2dYX2xhbXVKZm02QUNGd1VRQzRVTHh5UUNXRk1XYjllN0RfNHpUbGtwMnF2cHZqcEVValZNc1NvbC1QTTBfY1RIb3VYT1JPMlpucGJMV1RvOGlTc00?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE8yeGdBMXZQeHdkUUZ0UGlvRVM2LWtzTXpNaGVPT0JuYW1FWVZXUVZxall0S2hkcG1makZxUHp2aS1SNXNET0s2T3FTVXZFX2hoc1B2ZHVCMHlrRVc5THfSAWNBVV95cUxQbXZTdmkzWXpxci1iTDhkV3I1ZFVSNEtwM0pSbVMyRWxNUVlxM1RkSHRkRzZRWWtuNnU3RFVXenhmamtxNlZRX2VrYjVhX1F5SVNOWU5kVWg3bHFNeWF0TmxIQ0U?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Vanguard News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifkFVX3lxTE1PZ0JwdHh2cm5KZEU3X1VtX3FvYjlFekxOREh3UTM2WE5jWnM4blQxVWFVUktwVEFHOU5NVHF0T0JVVkRxREdwSFM0RjJTMVNEcGVYZFhtOEJWMGFuYngxTXFxQXlfRFVUMU9BZEVmZHFoR212NkZpVWZWTXpZZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Peoples Gazette Nigeria&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxPaFk1QmMxdG1PRENRZV9zTXRPUUtCa0x4ZHZkengtTnktdlRfZ25wRlNLM2E5YmxDRUlqZVoyRVkyc3djYzloUmtKYlRzYTZsUjVuX01aaFlFTmVVQ0M0UDF